reviews.text_contribution:
The author proposed a multi-modal pretraining mthod based on paired ultrasound images and medical report. By applying a VQA model, the proposed model can focus on specific pathological features in the pre-training task of image-text pairs；
Specifically, the author designs a quasi-textual feature space to help with bimodal feature alignment, in addition to using conventional contrastive learning for image-text pairs;
Experimental results demonstrate the superiority of the proposed methods in four downstreaming tasks, including report generation, classification, detection and segmentation.

reviews.text_detailed_comments:
The model performs well on all four downstreaming tasks. Three visual recognition related tasks results were displayed well in both visualize and numeric. But for the report generation task, it will be better to display some example cases because the text evaluation metrics are based on natural language, which may be not so suitable for medical report.

The main idea is relativly new;
Includes some engineering tricks, such as feature buffer and initialize methods;
Comprehensive experiments and large performance gains over other methods.

